# Publishable skills authoring

Consumer skills live under **`skills/<name>/`** in this repo. Distribute via `npx skills add equinusocio/react-authoring-skills`.

Editing skills? Follow Agent Skills checklist below.

## Required flow

1. Follow [agentskills.io/best-practices](https://agentskills.io/skill-creation/best-practices) and [agentskills.io/specification](https://agentskills.io/specification): thin hub, trigger-only description, progressive disclosure into sibling refs.
2. **RED before GREEN:** write or refresh `evals/<skill>/trigger_queries.json` and `evals.json` **before** editing `SKILL.md`.
3. Hub `description`: starts `Use when…`, ≤ 1024 chars, **triggers/symptoms only** — no workflow summary (see [optimizing-descriptions](https://agentskills.io/skill-creation/optimizing-descriptions)).
4. Hub frontmatter: `name`, `description`, then `license: MIT` and `metadata` (`author`, `version` semver string).
5. Hub body ~80–120 lines: router + hard contract + out of scope; refs are load-on-demand (“Read `foo.md` when …”).
6. Same change: update [README.md](README.md) Skills table when name/path/trigger changes; discipline skills need red-flag + rationalization tables.
7. Evals stay under `evals/<skill>/` — **never** under `skills/`.

## Before done

- Diff description against `trigger_queries.json` (true triggers vs near-miss false).
- Confirm hub frontmatter has `license: MIT` and `metadata.author` / `metadata.version`.
- Confirm README install still cites `npx skills add equinusocio/react-authoring-skills`.
- Keep hub thin; put deep guidance in sibling `.md` refs under the skill folder.

## Red flags — STOP

- “Skip evals — small hub tweak”
- “Put evals next to SKILL.md under `skills/`”
- “Description can summarize the workflow — agents read the body anyway”
- “README Skills table update later”
- “Document npm package / tarball install”

**All of these mean: complete the checklist in this change.**
